&lt;p&gt;The table above comes from Auntie Tintinalli's pillow (yes, the Tintinalli textbook) &lt;sup id="fnref1:1"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:1" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The most common causes of syncope are vasovagal (21%), cardiac (10%), orthostatic (9%), medication related (7%), neurologic (4%), and unknown (37%).&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>